<title>USA: Philadelphia Exchange to alter Semiconductor index.</title>
<headline>Philadelphia Exchange to alter Semiconductor index.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philadelphia Stock Exchange said it plans to add two computer chip companies and a semiconductor equipment maker to its Semiconductor Index .SOXX and remove three stocks currently listed on the index.</p>
<p>The exchange said it plans to add Linear Technology Corp, Xilinx Inc and Lam Research Corp.</p>
<p>Current components Cypress Semiconductor Corp, Integrated Device Technology Inc and International Rectifier Corp will be dropped from the 16-issue index.</p>
<p>The 13 other stocks that comprise the index remain unchanged.</p>
<p>The changes will become effective at the opening of trading on January 20, 1997, the exchange said.</p>
<p>((E. Auchard, Wall Street bureau, 212-859-1736))</p>
</text>
